window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-3c6726ad641677d6"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"sites\">Sites（网站）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>Sites 让你可以通过在 ChatGPT 或 Codex 中描述需求来构建、托管和分享网站。无需编写代码即可开始。你也可以托管 Web 应用、游戏或已完成且兼容的项目，而不必另行配置部署环境。</p> <p>如果你属于某个组织，Sites 可以为团队提供一个查找答案、探索电子表格数据或逐步开展项目启动工作的空间。你可以从现有文档和数据开始，并在过程中提出修改要求。</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8zH_O74hZBw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">观看：直接在 ChatGPT 中构建并发布 Web 应用（需联网）</a></p> <pre><code>{\n  \"如需了解当前的可用性、价格、套餐信息和使用限制，请访问 \"\n}\n[{\"帮助中心\"}（需联网）](https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339)\n{\".\"}\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"explore-site-types\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"explore-ways-to-use-sites\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"sites_1\">探索 Sites 的使用方式</h2> <p>以下示例旨在启发你使用 Sites 构建项目。你可以了解几种常见模式、组合不同功能，或尝试自己的想法。</p> <p><a id=\"resource-hub\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">资源中心</h3> <p>资源中心可以按主题整理文档和链接，并提供搜索功能和简短说明，帮助人们找到所需内容。每个搜索结果都可以打开原始文档或网页。</p> <p><a id=\"example-use-cases\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_2\">使用示例</h4> <ul> <li>新员工入职门户</li> <li>团队政策与流程资料库</li> <li>产品发布资源中心</li> <li>客户培训与支持中心</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">员工资源中心示意图，包含搜索、主题分组、文档卡片和欢迎指南。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/hub.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>员工资源中心示意图，包含搜索、主题分组、文档卡片和欢迎指南。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/hub.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"how-you-might-build-it\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_3\">构建思路</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>提供哪些内容</strong> 提供带有标题、简短说明和类别的文档或链接。说明资源中心面向哪些人，以及要重点展示哪些资源。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>提出哪些要求</strong> 要求创建资源卡片、支持搜索标题和说明，并提供类别筛选。说明每张卡片要显示什么、点击后是打开源链接还是资源中心内的页面，以及如何更新列表。还要规定搜索无匹配结果时访问者会看到什么。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查哪些内容</strong> 搜索一个已知条目，将搜索与筛选组合使用，并尝试一次无匹配结果的搜索。确认目标访问者能够打开链接资源，也能在手机上浏览。</p> </li> </ol> <p><a id=\"dashboard\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">仪表板</h3> <p>仪表板可以在一个视图中组合摘要数据、图表和表格。筛选器可以让用户按日期范围、团队或类别查看并比较结果。</p> <p><a id=\"example-use-cases_1\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_5\">使用示例</h4> <ul> <li>营销活动表现</li> <li>销售管线与预测</li> <li>客户支持量和响应时间</li> <li>产品采用情况与参与度</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">营销仪表板示意图，包含周期筛选、表现摘要、渠道对比和活动表格。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/dashboard.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>营销仪表板示意图，包含周期筛选、表现摘要、渠道对比和活动表格。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/dashboard.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"how-you-might-build-it_1\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_6\">构建思路</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>提供哪些内容</strong> 分享电子表格或数据样本。说明每一行和每一列的含义，并定义指标及其单位。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>提出哪些要求</strong> 要求提供摘要数据、图表以及带日期或类别筛选的明细表。说明哪些视图应同步更新，以及如何添加或刷新数据。规定筛选结果为空时要显示什么。缺失值应与零区分开；如果计算比率需要除以零，则应将该比率显示为不可用。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查哪些内容</strong> 在筛选前后，将总数和计算结果与源数据进行比较。测试无结果的筛选、缺失值，以及需要除以零才能计算的比率。确认每种情况都符合你规定的规则。</p> </li> </ol> <p><a id=\"tracker\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">跟踪器</h3> <p>跟踪器可以用表格记录任务或条目，并列出负责人、日期和状态标签。用户可以筛选所见内容，并更新自己有权限修改的条目。</p> <p><a id=\"example-use-cases_2\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_8\">使用示例</h4> <ul> <li>产品发布任务</li> <li>项目里程碑与依赖项</li> <li>编辑日历与内容审核</li> <li>客户入门进度</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">发布跟踪器示意图，包含任务表、负责人、截止日期、状态和阻碍事项。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/tracker.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>发布跟踪器示意图，包含任务表、负责人、截止日期、状态和阻碍事项。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/tracker.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"how-you-might-build-it_2\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_9\">构建思路</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>提供哪些内容</strong> 分享包含名称、负责人、日期和状态等字段的条目示例。说明状态标签的含义以及条目之间的依赖关系。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>提出哪些要求</strong> 要求创建表格或看板，支持按负责人和状态筛选，并提供添加或编辑条目的方式。规定何时将条目标记为逾期或受阻。说明更新应保存在哪里，以及谁可以查看或修改。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查哪些内容</strong> 添加或编辑一条记录，然后重新加载以确认更改已保存。测试每种状态和逾期日期。如果不同用户的访问权限不同，请使用不同账户检查谁可以查看和编辑条目。</p> </li> </ol> <p><a id=\"request-form\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">请求表单</h3> <p>请求表单可以通过输入字段、选项和附件收集详细信息。你可以要求它检查必填答案、保存提交内容供审核者查看，并显示说明后续步骤的确认信息。</p> <p><a id=\"example-use-cases_3\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_11\">使用示例</h4> <ul> <li>创意简报和设计请求</li> <li>活动与研讨会支持请求</li> <li>IT 和软件访问请求</li> <li>客户反馈提交</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">创意请求表单示意图，包含项目名称、简报、交付物、截止日期、附件和提交操作。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/intake.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>创意请求表单示意图，包含项目名称、简报、交付物、截止日期、附件和提交操作。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/intake.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"how-you-might-build-it_3\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_12\">构建思路</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>提供哪些内容</strong> 分享表单模板或列出需要收集的信息。标记必填字段，并列出允许的选项和附件类型。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>提出哪些要求</strong> 要求检查必填字段和接受的格式，并显示说明如何修正的消息。指定哪些答案会触发后续问题。说明提交内容和附件应保存在哪里、谁可以审核，以及确认信息应如何告知表单提交者。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查哪些内容</strong> 提交一份完整表单，并确认目标审核者可以看到已保存的请求。将必填字段留空，并尝试输入无效内容，检查表单是否说明需要修正什么。如果包含上传文件，请确认审核者可以打开已保存的附件。</p> </li> </ol> <p><a id=\"calculator\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">计算器</h3> <p>计算器可以使用你提供的公式，将可编辑的输入值转换为估算结果。用户可以修改数值、比较不同情景，并查看每项结果旁的单位和假设条件。</p> <p><a id=\"example-use-cases_4\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_14\">使用示例</h4> <ul> <li>活动预算情景</li> <li>团队人员配置和工作量估算</li> <li>研讨会时长和分组人数</li> <li>项目时间线估算</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">容量规划器示意图，包含团队人数和工作量输入、容量估算、假设条件和情景对比。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/calculator.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>容量规划器示意图，包含团队人数和工作量输入、容量估算、假设条件和情景对比。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/calculator.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"how-you-might-build-it_4\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_15\">构建思路</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>提供哪些内容</strong> 分享公式、单位、假设条件，以及包含预期结果的计算示例。说明哪些输入可以修改，哪些值必须保持固定。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>提出哪些要求</strong> 要求提供带标签的输入字段或滑块、初始值和允许范围。显示结果及其单位和假设条件。规定输入为零、空白或超出范围时如何处理，包括何时显示错误或不可用结果。如果需要比较情景，请指定哪些结果应并排显示。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查哪些内容</strong> 输入你提供的计算示例并比较结果。更改一项输入，检查输出是否正确更新。尝试输入零、空白和超出范围的值，确认每种情况都会按你的要求响应。</p> </li> </ol> <p><a id=\"guided-process\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">引导式流程</h3> <p>引导式流程可以将任务拆分为多个步骤，并根据之前的回答调整问题。用户可以返回上一步、按需保存进度，最后生成你指定的简报、检查清单或其他结果。</p> <p><a id=\"example-use-cases_5\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_17\">使用示例</h4> <ul> <li>员工入职检查清单</li> <li>项目启动规划</li> <li>活动简报制定</li> <li>供应商审核与审批步骤</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">项目启动指南示意图，包含编号步骤、针对性规划问题、进度指示和下一步操作。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/process.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>项目启动指南示意图，包含编号步骤、针对性规划问题、进度指示和下一步操作。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/process.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"how-you-might-build-it_5\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_18\">构建思路</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>提供哪些内容</strong> 分享检查清单或流程大纲。按顺序排列步骤，标记必答内容，并说明某个选项会如何导向不同问题。提供一份最终结果示例。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>提出哪些要求</strong> 要求每次显示一个步骤，提供进度指示，并支持返回上一步而不丢失答案。定义最终输出、必答项留空时的处理方式，以及不再适用的答案应移除还是标记。如果要保存进度，请说明保存位置以及谁可以恢复进度。</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>检查哪些内容</strong> 尝试主流程及每个分支。先将必答项留空，再修改前面的选项。检查问题和输出是否更新，不再适用的答案是否已移除或标记。如果要求保存进度，请重新加载以确认流程可以恢复。</p> </li> </ol> <p>配图示例使用虚构内容。</p> <p><a id=\"sites-use-cases\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"sites_2\">Sites 使用案例</h2> <p>以下是一些可以使用 Sites 尝试的案例。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b0e7a45d11db50af\">从简报到交付，管理创意请求</a>：将创意简报模板转换为请求应用，让同事提交工作请求，设计人员……</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0e09d3699dec6a33\">构建入职门户</a>：将团队第一周计划转换为每日活动、资源链接和练习任务……</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-cec78ec9a80a4b51\">了解哪些营销活动带来了潜在客户</a>：将每周活动导出数据转换为仪表板，供团队比较潜在客户数量和……</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7daaec47a2ac640c\">构建黑客马拉松网站</a>：将活动简报和日程转换为网站，引导参与者完成注册……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"understand-limits-and-unsupported-uses\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_19\">了解限制和不支持的用途</h2> <p>Sites 会在其支持的运行时中托管 Web 体验。部分框架、专用网络、数据库、后台服务和托管模式不受支持。</p> <p>支持 HTTP、HTTPS 和 WebSocket；不支持原始 TCP 入站和出站连接。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>资源</th> <th>每个 Site 的存储限制</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>D1 数据库</td> <td>10 GB</td> </tr> <tr> <td>R2 对象存储</td> <td>无固定存储上限</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>有关当前的数据驻留覆盖范围和工作区要求，请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001338-managing-chatgpt-sites-for-your-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">为工作区管理 ChatGPT Sites（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>你可以通过第三方支付处理商销售商品或服务并收款。支付卡数据必须完全由该服务商收集和处理，不得由你的网站或 OpenAI 处理。其他金融交易仍然禁止。你需负责集成、履约、退款、客户支持和适用税费。具体要求请参阅 <a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/chatgpt-sites-terms/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites 条款（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>请勿使用 Sites 处理受保护的健康信息，面向未满 13 岁或未达到适用数字同意年龄的儿童，传播恶意软件、协助网络钓鱼、冒充个人或组织，或以其他方式违反 OpenAI 政策。</p> <p>有关当前限制和政策链接，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">创建和管理 ChatGPT Sites（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"next-up\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_20\">接下来</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-56e8c36f028eb49f\"><strong>创建网站</strong><br> 在 ChatGPT 或 Codex 中描述需求、构建并完善网站。</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2\"><strong>数据与连接</strong><br> 选择存储方式、添加登录功能并将应用连接到网站。</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59\"><strong>发布与分享</strong><br> 检查网站、选择受众并与编辑者协作。</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-8063f9ed486db057\"><strong>管理网站</strong><br> 查看分析数据、更改域名和设置，并管理网站版本。</a></p>","en":"<h1 id=\"sites\">Sites</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Sites lets you build, host, and share a website by describing it in ChatGPT or Codex. You can get started without writing any code. You can also host web apps, games, or a compatible project you've already built, without a separate deployment setup.</p> <p>If you're part of an organization, Sites can give your team a place to find answers, explore results from a spreadsheet, or walk through a project kickoff. Start with the documents and data you already have, and ask for changes as you go.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8zH_O74hZBw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Watch: Build and publish web apps directly in ChatGPT (online)</a></p> <pre><code>{\n  \"For current availability, pricing, plan information, and usage limits, visit our \"\n}\n[{\"Help Center\"} (online)](https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339)\n{\".\"}\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"explore-site-types\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"explore-ways-to-use-sites\">Explore ways to use sites</h2> <p>The examples below are just inspiration for what you can build with Sites. Explore a few common patterns, combine their features, or try an idea of your own.</p> <h3 id=\"resource-hub\">Resource hub</h3> <p>A resource hub could group documents and links by topic, with search and short descriptions to help people find what they need. Each result might open the original document or page.</p> <h4 id=\"example-use-cases\">Example use cases</h4> <ul> <li>New employee onboarding portal</li> <li>Team policy and procedure library</li> <li>Product launch resource center</li> <li>Customer training and support hub</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Illustrative employee resource hub with search, topic groups, document cards, and a welcome guide. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/hub.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Illustrative employee resource hub with search, topic groups, document cards, and a welcome guide. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/hub.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h4 id=\"how-you-might-build-it\">How you might build it</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>What to share</strong> Provide documents or links with titles, short descriptions, and categories. Say who will use the hub and which resources to feature.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to ask for</strong> Ask for resource cards, search across titles and descriptions, and category filters. Specify what each card shows, whether it opens a source link or a page in the hub, and how the list should be updated. Define what visitors see when a search has no matches.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to check</strong> Search for a known item, combine a search with a filter, and try a search with no matches. Check that an intended visitor can open the linked resources and browse on a phone.</p> </li> </ol> <h3 id=\"dashboard\">Dashboard</h3> <p>A dashboard could combine summary numbers, charts, and tables in one view. Filters might let people explore a date range, team, or category and compare the results.</p> <h4 id=\"example-use-cases_1\">Example use cases</h4> <ul> <li>Marketing campaign performance</li> <li>Sales pipeline and forecast</li> <li>Customer support volume and response times</li> <li>Product adoption and engagement</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Illustrative marketing dashboard with period filters, performance summaries, channel comparisons, and a campaign table. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/dashboard.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Illustrative marketing dashboard with period filters, performance summaries, channel comparisons, and a campaign table. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/dashboard.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h4 id=\"how-you-might-build-it_1\">How you might build it</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>What to share</strong> Share a spreadsheet or sample of your data. Explain what each row and column means, and define the metrics and units.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to ask for</strong> Ask for summary numbers, charts, and a detail table with date or category filters. Specify which views should update together and how new data should be added or refreshed. Define what to show when a filter has no results. Keep missing values distinct from zero, and show a rate as unavailable if it would require dividing by zero.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to check</strong> Compare totals and calculations with the source data before and after filtering. Try a filter with no results, a missing value, and a rate that would require dividing by zero. Confirm each follows the rules you specified.</p> </li> </ol> <h3 id=\"tracker\">Tracker</h3> <p>A tracker could keep tasks or items in a table, with owners, dates, and status labels. People might filter what they see and update the items they have permission to change.</p> <h4 id=\"example-use-cases_2\">Example use cases</h4> <ul> <li>Product launch tasks</li> <li>Project milestones and dependencies</li> <li>Editorial calendar and content reviews</li> <li>Customer onboarding progress</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Illustrative launch tracker with a task table, owners, due dates, status, and blockers. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/tracker.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Illustrative launch tracker with a task table, owners, due dates, status, and blockers. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/tracker.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h4 id=\"how-you-might-build-it_2\">How you might build it</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>What to share</strong> Share sample items with fields such as name, owner, date, and status. Explain your status labels and any dependencies between items.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to ask for</strong> Ask for a table or board, filters by owner and status, and a way to add or edit items. Define when an item should be marked overdue or blocked. Say where updates should be saved and who should be able to view or change them.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to check</strong> Add or edit an item, then reload to confirm the change was saved. Try each status and an overdue date. If access differs by person, use separate accounts to check who can view and edit items.</p> </li> </ol> <h3 id=\"request-form\">Request form</h3> <p>A request form could collect details through fields, choices, and attachments. You might ask it to check required answers, save submissions for reviewers, and show a confirmation explaining what happens next.</p> <h4 id=\"example-use-cases_3\">Example use cases</h4> <ul> <li>Creative briefs and design requests</li> <li>Event and workshop support requests</li> <li>IT and software access requests</li> <li>Customer feedback submissions</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Illustrative creative request form with project name, brief, deliverables, due date, attachments, and a submit action. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/intake.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Illustrative creative request form with project name, brief, deliverables, due date, attachments, and a submit action. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/intake.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h4 id=\"how-you-might-build-it_3\">How you might build it</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>What to share</strong> Share a form template or list the details to collect. Mark required fields and list allowed choices and attachments.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to ask for</strong> Ask for checks on required fields and accepted formats, with messages explaining what to fix. Specify which answers trigger follow-up questions. Say where submissions and attachments should be saved, who can review them, and what the confirmation should tell the person who submitted the form.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to check</strong> Submit a complete form and confirm the saved request is available to the intended reviewers. Leave a required field blank and try an invalid entry to check that the form explains what to fix. If you included uploads, confirm reviewers can open the saved attachment.</p> </li> </ol> <h3 id=\"calculator\">Calculator</h3> <p>A calculator could turn editable inputs into an estimate using formulas you provide. People might change the numbers, compare scenarios, and see the units and assumptions beside each result.</p> <h4 id=\"example-use-cases_4\">Example use cases</h4> <ul> <li>Event budget scenarios</li> <li>Team staffing and workload estimates</li> <li>Workshop duration and group sizes</li> <li>Project timeline estimates</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Illustrative capacity planner with team size and workload inputs, capacity estimates, assumptions, and scenario comparisons. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/calculator.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Illustrative capacity planner with team size and workload inputs, capacity estimates, assumptions, and scenario comparisons. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/calculator.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h4 id=\"how-you-might-build-it_4\">How you might build it</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>What to share</strong> Share the formula, units, assumptions, and a worked example with its expected result. Explain which inputs people can change and which values should stay fixed.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to ask for</strong> Ask for labeled input fields or sliders, starting values, and allowed ranges. Show results with their units and assumptions. Define what happens for zero, blank, and out-of-range inputs, including when to show an error or an unavailable result. If people should compare scenarios, specify which results to show side by side.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to check</strong> Enter your worked example and compare the result. Change one input to check that the output updates correctly. Try zero, blank, and out-of-range values, and confirm each shows the response you specified.</p> </li> </ol> <h3 id=\"guided-process\">Guided process</h3> <p>A guided process could break a task into steps, with questions that change based on earlier answers. People might go back, save progress if needed, and finish with a brief, checklist, or other output you define.</p> <h4 id=\"example-use-cases_5\">Example use cases</h4> <ul> <li>Employee onboarding checklist</li> <li>Project kickoff planning</li> <li>Campaign brief development</li> <li>Vendor review and approval steps</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Illustrative project kickoff guide with numbered steps, focused planning questions, a progress indicator, and a next-step action. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/process.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Illustrative project kickoff guide with numbered steps, focused planning questions, a progress indicator, and a next-step action. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/sites/process.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h4 id=\"how-you-might-build-it_5\">How you might build it</h4> <ol> <li> <p><strong>What to share</strong> Share a checklist or outline of the process. Put the steps in order, mark required answers, and explain where a choice should lead to different questions. Include an example of the finished output.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to ask for</strong> Ask for one step at a time, a progress indicator, and a way to go back without losing answers. Define the final output, what happens when a required answer is blank, and whether answers that no longer apply should be removed or flagged. If progress should be saved, say where and who can return to it.</p> </li> <li> <p><strong>What to check</strong> Try the main path and each branch. Leave a required answer blank, then change an earlier choice. Check that questions and the output update, and answers that no longer apply are removed or flagged. If you requested saved progress, reload to confirm it resumes.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Illustrated examples with fictional content.</p> <h2 id=\"sites-use-cases\">Sites use cases</h2> <p>Here are some example use cases you can try with Sites.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b0e7a45d11db50af\">Manage creative requests from brief to delivery</a>: Turn your creative brief template into a request app where colleagues submit work, designers...</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0e09d3699dec6a33\">Build an onboarding portal</a>: Turn your team's first-week plan into daily activities, resource links, and a practice task...</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-cec78ec9a80a4b51\">See which campaigns bring in leads</a>: Turn weekly campaign exports into a dashboard where your team can compare lead volume and...</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7daaec47a2ac640c\">Build a hackathon site</a>: Turn your event brief and agenda into a site that guides participants through registration...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"understand-limits-and-unsupported-uses\">Understand limits and unsupported uses</h2> <p>Sites hosts web experiences in its supported runtime. Some frameworks, private networks, databases, background services, and hosting patterns aren't supported.</p> <p>HTTP, HTTPS, and WebSockets are supported. Raw inbound and outbound TCP connections aren't supported.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Resource</th> <th>Storage limit per site</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>D1 database</td> <td>10 GB</td> </tr> <tr> <td>R2 object storage</td> <td>No fixed storage limit</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For current residency coverage and workspace requirements, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001338-managing-chatgpt-sites-for-your-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Managing ChatGPT Sites for your workspace (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <p>You can sell goods or services and collect payments through a third-party payment processor. Payment-card data must be collected and processed solely by that provider, not by your site or OpenAI. Other financial transactions remain prohibited. You're responsible for the integration, fulfillment, refunds, customer support, and applicable taxes. See the <a href=\"https://openai.com/policies/chatgpt-sites-terms/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sites Terms (online)</a> for requirements.</p> <p>Don't use sites to process Protected Health Information; target children under 13 or the applicable age of digital consent; distribute malware; enable phishing; impersonate people or organizations; or otherwise violate OpenAI policies.</p> <p>See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001339\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and managing ChatGPT sites (online)</a> for current limits and policy links.</p> <h2 id=\"next-up\">Next up</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-56e8c36f028eb49f\"><strong>Create a site</strong><br> Describe, build, and refine a website in ChatGPT or Codex.</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-e0f092cc982945c2\"><strong>Data and connections</strong><br> Choose storage, add sign-in, and connect apps to your site.</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59\"><strong>Publish and share</strong><br> Review your site, choose its audience, and collaborate with editors.</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-8063f9ed486db057\"><strong>Manage a site</strong><br> Review analytics, change domains and settings, and manage site versions.</a></p>"};
